<title>USA: Total cuts U.S. posted crude prices 50 cts.</title>
<headline>Total cuts U.S. posted crude prices 50 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total Petroleum NA Ltd, a unit of Paris-based Total SA, said it lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $17.00 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $14.25 a barrel.</p>
<p>Oklahoma sweet is also $17.00, the company said.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623</p>
